(678665, 71114, 20037, '<td valign="top">Awesome capture of a moment.  Slight focus issues on the nose and some motion blur, bump up your iso and move to a faster shutter.  The head is dominating the frame a bit much for my taste - give a tad more headroom.  All in all excellent! (7)</td>', 'Awesome capture of a moment.  Slight focus issues on the nose and some motion blur, bump up your iso and move to a faster shutter.  The head is dominating the frame a bit much for my taste - give a tad more headroom.  All in all excellent! (7)', '2004-04-21 02:53:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(678668, 71255, 20037, '<td valign="top">This is a beautiful image.  Wonderful color treatment w/ the yellow on orange/red.  ONLY complaint is would like to see greater depth of field for bigger circles of confusion in the background to pop out the foreground a bit more.  Would like the whole foreground to be in focus - brush away those leaves in the front!  There is some purple in the top left corner that would have been an excellent contrast to the colors in the front.  I can almost smell the tea...mmmmmmmmmm. (8)</td>', 'This is a beautiful image.  Wonderful color treatment w/ the yellow on orange/red.  ONLY complaint is would like to see greater depth of field for bigger circles of confusion in the background to pop out the foreground a bit more.  Would like the whole foreground to be in focus - brush away those leaves in the front!  There is some purple in the top left corner that would have been an excellent contrast to the colors in the front.  I can almost smell the tea...mmmmmmmmmm. (8)', '2004-04-21 02:55:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(678672, 70954, 20037, '<td valign="top">OK first of all I want to say I love this image.  It''s definately in my top 10.  Here''s the few minor things I would change...get more of the vines in the shot, that green is compelling and I would love to have a bit more.  Crop out the roof and wires in the top right, the opposing lines are taking away from the vertical direction the wall panels are providing.  Or if you can work the roof in, shoot on a day w/ a clear blue sky to get a strong 3rd primary color in the shot - the blue/green/rust colors will play together nicely.  All in all, awesome (8)</td>', 'OK first of all I want to say I love this image.  It''s definately in my top 10.  Here''s the few minor things I would change...get more of the vines in the shot, that green is compelling and I would love to have a bit more.  Crop out the roof and wires in the top right, the opposing lines are taking away from the vertical direction the wall panels are providing.  Or if you can work the roof in, shoot on a day w/ a clear blue sky to get a strong 3rd primary color in the shot - the blue/green/rust colors will play together nicely.  All in all, awesome (8)', '2004-04-21 02:58:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(678675, 71277, 20037, '<td valign="top">This gives me a headache in a good way :)  Normally I don''t like shots like this but this is very well done, would like to get more definition of what is being reflected. (7)</td>', 'This gives me a headache in a good way :)  Normally I don''t like shots like this but this is very well done, would like to get more definition of what is being reflected. (7)', '2004-04-21 02:59:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(678678, 71280, 20037, '<td valign="top">Great use of color in the candies.  The out of focus seats are making me feel clastrophobic, which maybe was your intention but I feel like the "cieling and floor" are closing in on me.  I would try to at least get one of them in focus.  Also I''m having trouble "finding north" ....which way is up and down, also due to the DoF, that is probably another unsettling thing about this pic.  I do like it thou (7)</td>', 'Great use of color in the candies.  The out of focus seats are making me feel clastrophobic, which maybe was your intention but I feel like the "cieling and floor" are closing in on me.  I would try to at least get one of them in focus.  Also I''m having trouble "finding north" ....which way is up and down, also due to the DoF, that is probably another unsettling thing about this pic.  I do like it thou (7)', '2004-04-21 03:02:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(678683, 71254, 20037, '<td valign="top">Good choice to go B&amp;W with this image.  Maybe add a black border?  Also to solve the light reflection in the eyes problem, an fun trick I learned was if you get a bundle of standard issue christmas lights (like you put on your tree), and leave them on the "rack" they come in, you can create amazing "twinkles" in a person''s eye by casting hundreds of tiny points of light.  It also provides a great soft fill light if you ever need it because it falls off quickly. (7)</td>', 'Good choice to go B&W with this image.  Maybe add a black border?  Also to solve the light reflection in the eyes problem, an fun trick I learned was if you get a bundle of standard issue christmas lights (like you put on your tree), and leave them on the "rack" they come in, you can create amazing "twinkles" in a person''s eye by casting hundreds of tiny points of light.  It also provides a great soft fill light if you ever need it because it falls off quickly. (7)', '2004-04-21 03:05:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(678685, 71305, 20037, '<td valign="top">Am of course interested to see your details of how you got this shot!  Great idea too.  I''m not hot on the border choice.  A slight gradiant background of black/white could serve this well...(7)</td>', 'Am of course interested to see your details of how you got this shot!  Great idea too.  I''m not hot on the border choice.  A slight gradiant background of black/white could serve this well...(7)', '2004-04-21 03:06:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(678687, 71316, 20037, '<td valign="top">great image!  Would like the ground to either be completely in focus or out.  DoF would pop these suckers off the page nicely.  Saturate more to contrast the yellow wth the brown!  Well done. (7)</td>', 'great image!  Would like the ground to either be completely in focus or out.  DoF would pop these suckers off the page nicely.  Saturate more to contrast the yellow wth the brown!  Well done. (7)', '2004-04-21 03:07:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(678688, 70259, 20037, '<td valign="top">I bet this image will be a love/hate for most.  I personally love the simplicity of it.  My minor suggestions: Overexpose more, and blow out the sky slightly in B&amp;W to knock out those clouds and accentuate the differing contrasts of the sands.  Lower the angle to bring more of the fence into the sky for greater contrast of white to dark. (7)</td>', 'I bet this image will be a love/hate for most.  I personally love the simplicity of it.  My minor suggestions: Overexpose more, and blow out the sky slightly in B&W to knock out those clouds and accentuate the differing contrasts of the sands.  Lower the angle to bring more of the fence into the sky for greater contrast of white to dark. (7)', '2004-04-21 03:09:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(678691, 70653, 20037, '<td valign="top">Simply beautiful.  Kudos for even finding our ladybug friend.  My minor feedback: would like to see a bit more contrast/exposure.  Zoom in slightly to focus more attention to the bug - I almost missed her the first pass! (7)</td>', 'Simply beautiful.  Kudos for even finding our ladybug friend.  My minor feedback: would like to see a bit more contrast/exposure.  Zoom in slightly to focus more attention to the bug - I almost missed her the first pass! (7)', '2004-04-21 03:11:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(678694, 70722, 20037, '<td valign="top">Wow, amazing, I can''t wait to see where this is from.  Would like to see a higher angle and get more of the sea below. (7)</td>', 'Wow, amazing, I can''t wait to see where this is from.  Would like to see a higher angle and get more of the sea below. (7)', '2004-04-21 03:12:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(678695, 70711, 19780, '<td valign="top">Lovely shot. I like the color and texture of the brick wall. I wish the plants in the pipes were healthier so as the make the serendipity point better but I still give it very high marks.</td>', 'Lovely shot. I like the color and texture of the brick wall. I wish the plants in the pipes were healthier so as the make the serendipity point better but I still give it very high marks.', '2004-04-21 03:12:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(678697, 71113, 20037, '<td valign="top">Hard to watch but a powerful image.  Bravo.  Could a few moments after this when the calf was just born be as powerful and more tender?  Great focus on this shot. (7)</td>', 'Hard to watch but a powerful image.  Bravo.  Could a few moments after this when the calf was just born be as powerful and more tender?  Great focus on this shot. (7)', '2004-04-21 03:14:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(678698, 70696, 19780, '<td valign="top">A wonderful photo - great perspective, I love the reclaimed nature of the bridge and the placement of the person on it. I wonder about how well it fits the assignment, but I gave it my highest mark, I''m glad you chose black and white.</td>', 'A wonderful photo - great perspective, I love the reclaimed nature of the bridge and the placement of the person on it. I wonder about how well it fits the assignment, but I gave it my highest mark, I''m glad you chose black and white.', '2004-04-21 03:15:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(678701, 71107, 20037, '<td valign="top">Wonderful color treatment.  Amazing to catch the raindrops just so.  Pointing out the obvious: some blur on her cost.  Too much negative space for me - she''s gourgeous and should be focused on, plus you''re getting more bang for the buck on the raindrops around her shadow. In my top 5, easily (8)</td>', 'Wonderful color treatment.  Amazing to catch the raindrops just so.  Pointing out the obvious: some blur on her cost.  Too much negative space for me - she''s gourgeous and should be focused on, plus you''re getting more bang for the buck on the raindrops around her shadow. In my top 5, easily (8)', '2004-04-21 03:16:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(678703, 71308, 20037, '<td valign="top">Way to capture the moment. (7)</td>', 'Way to capture the moment. (7)', '2004-04-21 03:16:55.000000', NULL, 1),
