(679102, 70314, 9295, '<td valign="top">I love that you took a different point of view regarding the money theme. Finding a family picture within the bills is a nice change from the many shots showing money found in books or gardening or whatever.  Not only is the theme nice, but I also like the quality of the photo itself. The composition, depth of field, sepia, lighting...all very nice. One of my favorites.</td>', 'I love that you took a different point of view regarding the money theme. Finding a family picture within the bills is a nice change from the many shots showing money found in books or gardening or whatever.  Not only is the theme nice, but I also like the quality of the photo itself. The composition, depth of field, sepia, lighting...all very nice. One of my favorites.', '2004-04-21 09:28:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(679104, 70842, 14255, '<td valign="top">Or the wrong time !!! What made the splash?</td>', 'Or the wrong time !!! What made the splash?', '2004-04-21 09:28:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(679111, 71291, 4285, '<td valign="top">Finally, something caught that was not staged. Good capture. If you''re like me you are limited by you''re lens; if you don''t have a telephoto lens (ex. 75-300mm) there''s not alot you can do to make your DOF shallower. Would have been a better capture with just the deer''s head in sharp focus, that way the trees and other elements wouldn''t have been so distracting. Also I find that it has a slight purple colour cast; you can remove this in Photoshop in levels using the gray eyedropper by sampling something gray in the image; with an image like this it is mostly trial and error because you don''t have something "controlled" like an 18% gray card to sample.</td>', 'Finally, something caught that was not staged. Good capture. If you''re like me you are limited by you''re lens; if you don''t have a telephoto lens (ex. 75-300mm) there''s not alot you can do to make your DOF shallower. Would have been a better capture with just the deer''s head in sharp focus, that way the trees and other elements wouldn''t have been so distracting. Also I find that it has a slight purple colour cast; you can remove this in Photoshop in levels using the gray eyedropper by sampling something gray in the image; with an image like this it is mostly trial and error because you don''t have something "controlled" like an 18% gray card to sample.', '2004-04-21 09:35:48.000000', NULL, 1),
