(688781, 71305, 16406, '<td valign="top">in no way the boundary between the 2 images has been made with a game card... too soft line... and in no way it''s a double exposure... the two images are mixed here in the same level (or layer maybe... ?)<br/> <br/>the image is stunning.. but if dpchallenge is accepting manipulated photo on basic challenge, then i will change my way to post....<br/> <br/>can you post the raw somewhere please?</td>', 'in no way the boundary between the 2 images has been made with a game card... too soft line... and in no way it''s a double exposure... the two images are mixed here in the same level (or layer maybe... ?) the image is stunning.. but if dpchallenge is accepting manipulated photo on basic challenge, then i will change my way to post.... can you post the raw somewhere please?', '2004-04-28 10:15:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(688803, 71305, 7687, '<td valign="top">Great work, very creative.<br/> <br/>By "double exposure" the photograper means, exposing two subjects in the same frame, not opening the shutter twice.  <br/> <br/>It''s really very simple if you think about it.  By holding a piece of paper/cardboard directly over the lens, one half of the CCD doesn''t receive any light, then after reaching the proper exposure with one side, you slide the cardboard over and expose the yet to be exposed side.  <br/> <br/>If you simply think out of the box, you''ll get it.<br/> <br/>Again, excellent work.</td>', 'Great work, very creative. By "double exposure" the photograper means, exposing two subjects in the same frame, not opening the shutter twice.   It''s really very simple if you think about it.  By holding a piece of paper/cardboard directly over the lens, one half of the CCD doesn''t receive any light, then after reaching the proper exposure with one side, you slide the cardboard over and expose the yet to be exposed side.   If you simply think out of the box, you''ll get it. Again, excellent work.', '2004-04-28 10:27:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(688809, 71197, 19841, '<td valign="top">I love it.  I don''t think it''s seredipity, though; I EXPECT to find a cat in the sink. ;)</td>', 'I love it.  I don''t think it''s seredipity, though; I EXPECT to find a cat in the sink. ;)', '2004-04-28 10:32:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(688836, 70507, 19670, '<td valign="top">After reading much about serendipty in the forums and what Kavey said, I retract my earlier comment and now admit that this is a good example of a serendipity shot. Nice photo!</td>', 'After reading much about serendipty in the forums and what Kavey said, I retract my earlier comment and now admit that this is a good example of a serendipity shot. Nice photo!', '2004-04-28 10:44:01.000000', NULL, 0),
