(697914, 71210, 14986, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This is a fun entry!  Who hasn''t dreamed of instant fortune?  I like the composition of the photo.   There is no question what the shot is meant to be about.  The placement of the large "LOTTO" text brings the subject out immediately. <br/> <br/>Of course you have all the voters wondering if this actually happened!  I''d say you probably printed up the report behind the ticket to use as a prop for the shot.  I think it''s done very effectively.  The placement of the pen, the circling of the numbers...it all adds up to a wonderful serendipity shot.   <br/> <br/>As for meeting the challenge....hmm, that''s a tough question with this challenge.  I guess it doesn''t quite meet my own definition for serendipity, but it''s close.  It strikes me more as luck.<br/> <br/>Technically, I think it''s very well done.  Good focus, lighting, and colors.  I can''t think of anything that I would like to see done differently.<br/> <br/>Great job!<br/> <br/>I hope you find this helpful.</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club! This is a fun entry!  Who hasn''t dreamed of instant fortune?  I like the composition of the photo.   There is no question what the shot is meant to be about.  The placement of the large "LOTTO" text brings the subject out immediately.  Of course you have all the voters wondering if this actually happened!  I''d say you probably printed up the report behind the ticket to use as a prop for the shot.  I think it''s done very effectively.  The placement of the pen, the circling of the numbers...it all adds up to a wonderful serendipity shot.    As for meeting the challenge....hmm, that''s a tough question with this challenge.  I guess it doesn''t quite meet my own definition for serendipity, but it''s close.  It strikes me more as luck. Technically, I think it''s very well done.  Good focus, lighting, and colors.  I can''t think of anything that I would like to see done differently. Great job! I hope you find this helpful.', '2004-05-04 23:34:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(697971, 70604, 6900, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club (and America)<br/> <br/>I wish I could see the front of the statue in this shot.  There is a lack of context for the shot that makes it not much more than a statue in a corner.  I like the clouds in the shot, but it doesn''t feel .. whole.  Maybe like something is missing?<br/> <br/>Oh, and the statement is excellent - whether I agree with you or not (I don''t), you DID something with your photo.  It MEANS something.  That''s worth a lot.<br/> <br/>Mav</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club (and America) I wish I could see the front of the statue in this shot.  There is a lack of context for the shot that makes it not much more than a statue in a corner.  I like the clouds in the shot, but it doesn''t feel .. whole.  Maybe like something is missing? Oh, and the statement is excellent - whether I agree with you or not (I don''t), you DID something with your photo.  It MEANS something.  That''s worth a lot. Mav', '2004-05-05 00:00:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(697984, 71272, 6900, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This was a hard challenge.  Serendipity can mean this - finding money growing on a tree.  However, this SHOT was not serendipitous.  You planted it and thus it violates the SPIRIT of the challenge, if not the rule.  As to the pic itself - why not put the money on a tree bud?  Like it''s actually "growing on trees."  Or something similar.<br/> <br/>The lighting is kinda flat and overall the shot could use a bit more interest.  I like the idea, but it could use refining.<br/> <br/>Happy shooting,<br/>Mav</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! This was a hard challenge.  Serendipity can mean this - finding money growing on a tree.  However, this SHOT was not serendipitous.  You planted it and thus it violates the SPIRIT of the challenge, if not the rule.  As to the pic itself - why not put the money on a tree bud?  Like it''s actually "growing on trees."  Or something similar. The lighting is kinda flat and overall the shot could use a bit more interest.  I like the idea, but it could use refining. Happy shooting,Mav', '2004-05-05 00:08:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(697995, 71327, 6900, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>I think I can see two things I love about this photo and two things I could change to improve it.<br/> <br/>Loves:<br/>1. I''m a silhouette lover.  The silhouettes of the crosses and the meaning your title attaches to them is excellent.  Whether or not I agree with your intent here doesn''t matter.  You''ve created an emotive photo - one that is more than just run of the mill stock photography.<br/>2. The sky color is brilliant.  Yellows instead of reds are really nice to see occassionally in a sunset photo.  Nice originality.<br/> <br/>Disloves:<br/>1. The contrast hurts my eyes as well.  It''s a bit much at some point.  Not sure how I''d change that though.  A tiny bit less contrast or a slightly better exposure metering the sun itself?<br/>2. The crop is kind of far away.  I would move in on the sun/crosses and get rid of chunks of blackness - I don''t think it would hurt your theme to have a bit less black around the bottom.<br/> <br/>Happy shooting!<br/> <br/>Mav</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! I think I can see two things I love about this photo and two things I could change to improve it. Loves:1. I''m a silhouette lover.  The silhouettes of the crosses and the meaning your title attaches to them is excellent.  Whether or not I agree with your intent here doesn''t matter.  You''ve created an emotive photo - one that is more than just run of the mill stock photography.2. The sky color is brilliant.  Yellows instead of reds are really nice to see occassionally in a sunset photo.  Nice originality. Disloves:1. The contrast hurts my eyes as well.  It''s a bit much at some point.  Not sure how I''d change that though.  A tiny bit less contrast or a slightly better exposure metering the sun itself?2. The crop is kind of far away.  I would move in on the sun/crosses and get rid of chunks of blackness - I don''t think it would hurt your theme to have a bit less black around the bottom. Happy shooting! Mav', '2004-05-05 00:12:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(698000, 71235, 6900, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This is a shot I don''t get.  When I saw where it placed, I was stunned.  I am surprised that it beat a number of shots it beat.  On second look, I think I know why.<br/> <br/>This is a really decent, average photo (5.2ish) but there is one glaring weakness: that overexposed bit of it.  That part ruins the whole photo for me, but obviously when people voted, they took into consideration the photo as a whole.  I wish I''d been able to do that at the time.  Your focus is on, the colors are nice - but that spot is so overly distracting that people aren''t going to see what''s good about it.<br/> <br/>Oh, and did you mean Jewels?  I see you''re in Germany - still gotta check your spellings or the English speakers will eat your shot up just for that spelling mistake.<br/> <br/>Happy shooting and good luck<br/> <br/>Mav</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! This is a shot I don''t get.  When I saw where it placed, I was stunned.  I am surprised that it beat a number of shots it beat.  On second look, I think I know why. This is a really decent, average photo (5.2ish) but there is one glaring weakness: that overexposed bit of it.  That part ruins the whole photo for me, but obviously when people voted, they took into consideration the photo as a whole.  I wish I''d been able to do that at the time.  Your focus is on, the colors are nice - but that spot is so overly distracting that people aren''t going to see what''s good about it. Oh, and did you mean Jewels?  I see you''re in Germany - still gotta check your spellings or the English speakers will eat your shot up just for that spelling mistake. Happy shooting and good luck Mav', '2004-05-05 00:15:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(698014, 70323, 6900, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>I think two things hurt this image and one thing really really helped it.<br/> <br/>First, this image is a FANTASTIC action shot.  That is the best thing about it, and the thing you probably saw when you decided to enter it.  The spray is great, the action is caught at the exact right moment.<br/> <br/>Now, the problem is two-fold.  First of all, the serendipity of the shot is missed because we don''t know if you went to an event, if this is your friend, etc.  This could easily be a "posed" shot (setup shot) as well as something you just walked by and had to take the pic.<br/> <br/>Also, the image is a bit small.  Size the largest side to 640 pixels and let us see the details in such a great image.  Do that and you''d have a 5.5 on this shot.<br/> <br/>Mav</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! I think two things hurt this image and one thing really really helped it. First, this image is a FANTASTIC action shot.  That is the best thing about it, and the thing you probably saw when you decided to enter it.  The spray is great, the action is caught at the exact right moment. Now, the problem is two-fold.  First of all, the serendipity of the shot is missed because we don''t know if you went to an event, if this is your friend, etc.  This could easily be a "posed" shot (setup shot) as well as something you just walked by and had to take the pic. Also, the image is a bit small.  Size the largest side to 640 pixels and let us see the details in such a great image.  Do that and you''d have a 5.5 on this shot. Mav', '2004-05-05 00:23:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(698031, 71265, 6900, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Nice to meet you Andrew.<br/> <br/>I think one major point was underscored by a comment you received: the background is distracting.  You can''t always control these things, but if you are able to change your aperture or even the angle you shoot from, sometimes you can dramatically improve your composition just by focusing on the stuff around your main subject.  In this case, you took a wonderfully focused shot (don''t mind the ''blurry'' stuff - your subject is in focus) and just didn''t quite get there with the composition or technical quality.<br/> <br/>This is an interesting bug - I don''t think I''d like to see one like it. lol<br/> <br/>Mav</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Nice to meet you Andrew. I think one major point was underscored by a comment you received: the background is distracting.  You can''t always control these things, but if you are able to change your aperture or even the angle you shoot from, sometimes you can dramatically improve your composition just by focusing on the stuff around your main subject.  In this case, you took a wonderfully focused shot (don''t mind the ''blurry'' stuff - your subject is in focus) and just didn''t quite get there with the composition or technical quality. This is an interesting bug - I don''t think I''d like to see one like it. lol Mav', '2004-05-05 00:29:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(698053, 70576, 6900, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This picture seems a bit overexposed to me.  The leaf lacks much detail and the ground scene does seem contrived - a bit outside of the ''serendipity'' challenge, perhaps.<br/> <br/>I like the intent of your photo and yes, it does mostly take me back to LoTR but in LoTR the ring wasn''t found just sitting atop the ground like this.  Perhaps if this ring were half buried, sitting in black mud and shining out despite all of that - then the connotation may fully be there.<br/> <br/>Happy shooting,<br/> <br/>Mav</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! This picture seems a bit overexposed to me.  The leaf lacks much detail and the ground scene does seem contrived - a bit outside of the ''serendipity'' challenge, perhaps. I like the intent of your photo and yes, it does mostly take me back to LoTR but in LoTR the ring wasn''t found just sitting atop the ground like this.  Perhaps if this ring were half buried, sitting in black mud and shining out despite all of that - then the connotation may fully be there. Happy shooting, Mav', '2004-05-05 00:42:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(698059, 71313, 9581, '<td valign="top">Ok my first critique in awhile... I clicked on CC and 191 photos await! <br/>Then clicked on give me a image and I got lucky! <br/>Cause I got a photo I could relate too!<br/>and this challenge is over....<br/>Man why I did not vote on this one....Its a good one....<br/>Lets see to make it better, <br/>I would have another color background to bring out the guitar, its awesome brown havent seen electric like that...its really good DOF accept I think the hand on the left maybe a little more focus would help, but what do I know this is probably done while hes playing.... So really this is a great photo to me....its hard for me to give any constructive critism for it.......reading other comments now.....<br/> <br/>Lots of pros and cons.....and by the way...this is very original its yours...And I believe guitars and the hands should be the center or focus of a good still photograph been trying to master it myself.... like giving critiques in away! <br/>Dont give up !   and it must be late had to edit cross the t''s and dot the i''s......<br/>Anyways hope to see more of your photos here...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-05-05 00:31:56.</i></td>', 'Ok my first critique in awhile... I clicked on CC and 191 photos await! Then clicked on give me a image and I got lucky! Cause I got a photo I could relate too!and this challenge is over....Man why I did not vote on this one....Its a good one....Lets see to make it better, I would have another color background to bring out the guitar, its awesome brown havent seen electric like that...its really good DOF accept I think the hand on the left maybe a little more focus would help, but what do I know this is probably done while hes playing.... So really this is a great photo to me....its hard for me to give any constructive critism for it.......reading other comments now..... Lots of pros and cons.....and by the way...this is very original its yours...And I believe guitars and the hands should be the center or focus of a good still photograph been trying to master it myself.... like giving critiques in away! Dont give up !   and it must be late had to edit cross the t''s and dot the i''s......Anyways hope to see more of your photos here...', '2004-05-05 00:47:08.000000', '2004-05-05 01:31:56.000000', 0),
(698063, 70810, 6900, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>The focus on this shot could have been a bit better, though I am not familiar with your camera so perhaps it could not have been with your equipment.  This was a spectacular find, but if you could have just gotten it a bit sharper, it would have helped tremendously.<br/> <br/>I also think I don''t see the need for all the negative space at the bottom of this photo.  I would have cropped a bit tighter and used the fully 640 height to show the detail in the droplet.<br/> <br/>Happy shooting and good luck!<br/> <br/>Mav</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! The focus on this shot could have been a bit better, though I am not familiar with your camera so perhaps it could not have been with your equipment.  This was a spectacular find, but if you could have just gotten it a bit sharper, it would have helped tremendously. I also think I don''t see the need for all the negative space at the bottom of this photo.  I would have cropped a bit tighter and used the fully 640 height to show the detail in the droplet. Happy shooting and good luck! Mav', '2004-05-05 00:48:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(698070, 71107, 6900, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Nice to "meet" you Kali.<br/> <br/>What can I say about this shot?  It''s fantastic.  How come you didn''t get DQ''d when you submit your info?  *shrug*  Strange. <br/> <br/>Anyways - congrats on the purple ribbon.  I don''t think there''s much to critique here.  Maybe the top center of the photo is a tad overexposed?  Maybe the real problem is that I didn''t take this photo?  :)<br/> <br/>Good job and continued good luck!<br/> <br/>Mav</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Nice to "meet" you Kali. What can I say about this shot?  It''s fantastic.  How come you didn''t get DQ''d when you submit your info?  *shrug*  Strange.  Anyways - congrats on the purple ribbon.  I don''t think there''s much to critique here.  Maybe the top center of the photo is a tad overexposed?  Maybe the real problem is that I didn''t take this photo?  :) Good job and continued good luck! Mav', '2004-05-05 00:55:32.000000', NULL, 0),
