(709180, 70813, 19865, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Clangdon:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kali:</b></div><hr/><i> OMG, are you serious? You''ve got the phone backwards first of all.. speaker to speaker/ mic to mic. It almost feels like you''re purposefully trying to waste my time. 1 question.. Would you hang this on your wall as art? Ask yourself that next time before entering a challenge. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Jeeez, What did you have for breakfast this morning? Carnation Instant Bitch?! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>yeah. she is a real bitch, for sure. like she even did anything better. its just a purely envy and jealousy, fo uncapable perosn like this bitch</td>', 'Originally posted by Clangdon: Originally posted by Kali: OMG, are you serious? You''ve got the phone backwards first of all.. speaker to speaker/ mic to mic. It almost feels like you''re purposefully trying to waste my time. 1 question.. Would you hang this on your wall as art? Ask yourself that next time before entering a challenge.   Jeeez, What did you have for breakfast this morning? Carnation Instant Bitch?!   yeah. she is a real bitch, for sure. like she even did anything better. its just a purely envy and jealousy, fo uncapable perosn like this bitch', '2004-05-10 15:36:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(718579, 71083, 19708, '<td valign="top">Hi Judy,<br/>Thanks for the feedback.<br/>I tried so many variations of this shot it wasn''t funny.<br/>In order to get the details by being close enough, the angles changed. To step back and compress the shot would have meant standing out on a busy street.<br/>I cropped and rotated and cropped and rotated until I was sick of looking at this picture (LOL) and keeping withing the basic editing constraints, it''s was the best combination.<br/> <br/>Regards,</td>', 'Hi Judy,Thanks for the feedback.I tried so many variations of this shot it wasn''t funny.In order to get the details by being close enough, the angles changed. To step back and compress the shot would have meant standing out on a busy street.I cropped and rotated and cropped and rotated until I was sick of looking at this picture (LOL) and keeping withing the basic editing constraints, it''s was the best combination. Regards,', '2004-05-14 16:00:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(719825, 70696, 9441, '<td valign="top">this is such a cool shot!  Wonderful DOF.  Putting it in the sepia tone added a certain ''mood'' to this shot.  Nice job.</td>', 'this is such a cool shot!  Wonderful DOF.  Putting it in the sepia tone added a certain ''mood'' to this shot.  Nice job.', '2004-05-15 13:42:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(727588, 71274, 7364, '<td valign="top">Those women aren''t Asian!</td>', 'Those women aren''t Asian!', '2004-05-19 17:28:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(727771, 71342, 19305, '<td valign="top">All right. Since there seems to have been mass confusion as to what the image really is...<br/> <br/>I really was walking through the park in Ft. Wayne, Indiana, after dark with some friends. One of the parks that winds along the river. None of us had ever been to this particular park before. We turned a corner and there was this huge stainless steel park-type structure. It was shaped like a flying saucer with three support pilliars and some decorative metalwork coming up to it from the ground. It was illuminated with small blue and purple LEDs on the underside. There were also some recessed lights that were not turned on or burt out. It was part art part functional, serving as a large, tall gazebo over a water fountain. It was really random and surprised us all as it was so out of place and unexpected.<br/> <br/>My camera (yes a crappy cheapo, I know) has a mode where it fires the flash but keeps the shutter open for night portraits. I used this mode, exposed the basic shape and form of it with the flash and then moved the camera to blur the lights. I think the results looked pretty cool, especially for a $130 camera (hey, it''s pocketable!).</td>', 'All right. Since there seems to have been mass confusion as to what the image really is... I really was walking through the park in Ft. Wayne, Indiana, after dark with some friends. One of the parks that winds along the river. None of us had ever been to this particular park before. We turned a corner and there was this huge stainless steel park-type structure. It was shaped like a flying saucer with three support pilliars and some decorative metalwork coming up to it from the ground. It was illuminated with small blue and purple LEDs on the underside. There were also some recessed lights that were not turned on or burt out. It was part art part functional, serving as a large, tall gazebo over a water fountain. It was really random and surprised us all as it was so out of place and unexpected. My camera (yes a crappy cheapo, I know) has a mode where it fires the flash but keeps the shutter open for night portraits. I used this mode, exposed the basic shape and form of it with the flash and then moved the camera to blur the lights. I think the results looked pretty cool, especially for a $130 camera (hey, it''s pocketable!).', '2004-05-19 18:30:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(727789, 71274, 8522, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by lbWhaples:</b></div><hr/><i> Those women aren''t Asian! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Amazing how you''ve come to that conclusion, seeing as they''re taking part in an asian festival procession.</td>', 'Originally posted by lbWhaples: Those women aren''t Asian!   Amazing how you''ve come to that conclusion, seeing as they''re taking part in an asian festival procession.', '2004-05-19 18:38:15.000000', NULL, 0),
